  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat percentage of Faraday's flower-shop sales came from sunflower bouquets? Faraday owns a flower stall. Faraday's flower shop sold 50 bouquets during the week. 12 of the bouquets sold that week were sunflower bouquets.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. Find the fraction of bouquets that were sunflower bouquets:\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{50}\n\\]\n\n2. Convert the fraction to a percentage:\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{50}\\times 100 = 24\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Faraday owns a flower shop.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "No problem—the wording does not change the calculation. Faraday’s flower shop sold 50 bouquets, and 12 were sunflower bouquets:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{50}\\times 100=24\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many sunflower bouquets did Faraday sell per day on average during that week? Additionally, Faraday's flower shop was open for 6 days during that week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Faraday sold 12 sunflower bouquets over 6 days. The average per day was:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{6}=2\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\text{ sunflower bouquets per day}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Faraday sells individual sunflowers for $3 each.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Understood. Individual sunflowers sell for **$3 each**. Thus, if Faraday sold \\(n\\) individual sunflowers, the revenue would be:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$3n}\n\\]\n\nThe number of individual sunflowers sold hasn’t been specified yet.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many sunflowers was Faraday able to sell after three days? And here are a few things you should know: Faraday sells bouquets of sunflowers for $8 each. Faraday earns $26 per day from individual sunflowers and $56 per day from bouquets.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Faraday earned \\(\\$26\\) per day from individual sunflowers. Over 3 days:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times \\$26=\\$78\n\\]\n\nSince each individual sunflower sells for \\(\\$3\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\$78}{\\$3}=26\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Faraday sold:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{26\\text{ individual sunflowers}}\n\\]\n\nFor reference, the bouquet figures imply \\(56\\div 8=7\\) bouquets per day, or \\(21\\) bouquets over 3 days.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — Each bouquet contains 12 sunflowers.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Over 3 days:\n\n- **Individual sunflowers:**\n  \\[\n  \\frac{3\\times \\$26}{\\$3}=26\\text{ sunflowers}\n  \\]\n\n- **Sunflower bouquets:**\n  \\[\n  \\frac{\\$56}{\\$8}=7\\text{ bouquets per day}\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  7\\times 3=21\\text{ bouquets}\n  \\]\n  Each bouquet has 12 sunflowers:\n  \\[\n  21\\times 12=252\\text{ sunflowers}\n  \\]\n\nTotal sunflowers:\n\n\\[\n26+252=\\boxed{278\\text{ sunflowers}}\n\\]\n\nThis uses the daily earnings information; those figures differ from the earlier total of 12 sunflower bouquets for the week.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Faraday sells individual sunflowers for $2 each.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "With individual sunflowers priced at \\(\\$2\\) each:\n\n- Individual sunflowers sold in 3 days:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{3\\times \\$26}{\\$2}=\\frac{\\$78}{\\$2}=39\n  \\]\n\n- Bouquets sold in 3 days:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{3\\times \\$56}{\\$8}=21\n  \\]\n\n- Sunflowers in those bouquets:\n  \\[\n  21\\times 12=252\n  \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of sunflowers sold was:\n\n\\[\n39+252=\\boxed{291\\text{ sunflowers}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
